From: Armada <armada@armada.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom: add Eliza WPSS using existing PAS support

Reuse sc7280_wpss_resource, as Milos does. Qualcomm's downstream Kera
WPSS descriptor uses the same PAS ID (6), crash-reason SMEM (626),
minidump ID (4), load-state/SSR/sysmon name (wpss), and SSCTL ID (0x19).
The Duo Android tree votes CX and MX and uses the RPMh XO clock.

Reuse the Milos WPSS and SMP2P descriptions with the Duo Android capture's
register address (0x97000000) and watchdog SPI (200). SMP2P SMEM IDs
617/616, remote PID 13, IPCC client 24 and signal IDs match Milos.
The existing Eliza WPSS reserved memory also matches Android.

Keep the SoC node disabled by default. The shared PAS descriptor retains
auto_boot=false, leaving firmware startup to a consumer or an explicit
userspace request. No WLAN transport or data path is added.

Reference: OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_oneplus_sm8750,
  oneplus/sm8750_b_16.0.0_oneplus_13, drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c,
  kera_wpss_resource; verified against the Duo's Android FDT and boot log.

Ported from armada (armada-os/armada b91b786) 1114: the driver and binding half. The match entry sits
after mainline's new eliza-cdsp entry; the binding hunk after its
eliza-adsp. The DTS half is `1189`.
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/qcom,milos-pas.yaml | 2 ++
 drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c                               | 1 +
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/qcom,milos-pas.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/qcom,milos-pas.yaml
index b24e6f6ea..d844f5b9c 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/qcom,milos-pas.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/qcom,milos-pas.yaml
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@ description:
 properties:
   compatible:
     enum:
+      - qcom,eliza-wpss-pas
       - qcom,milos-adsp-pas
       - qcom,milos-cdsp-pas
       - qcom,milos-mpss-pas
@@ -123,6 +124,7 @@ allOf:
       properties:
         compatible:
           enum:
+            - qcom,eliza-wpss-pas
             - qcom,milos-cdsp-pas
             - qcom,milos-wpss-pas
     then:
diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
index 9f2367564..51cef2dca 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
@@ -2110,6 +2110,7 @@ static const struct qcom_pas_data eliza_cdsp_resource = {
 static const struct of_device_id qcom_pas_of_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,eliza-adsp-pas", .data = &sm8550_adsp_resource },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,eliza-cdsp-pas", .data = &eliza_cdsp_resource },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,eliza-wpss-pas", .data = &sc7280_wpss_resource },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,glymur-soccp-pas", .data = &glymur_soccp_resource },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,kaanapali-soccp-pas", .data = &kaanapali_soccp_resource },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,milos-adsp-pas", .data = &sm8550_adsp_resource },
